SUGIMOTO, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coryneform bacterium having an enhanced 6-phosphofuructokinase activity in cell and being capable of producing L-lysine; a process for producing L-lysine characterized by comprising culturing the above coryneform bacterium in a medium, thus forming and accumulating L-lysine in the culture medium, and collecting the L-lysine from the culture medium; and a DNA usable in enhancing the 6-phosphofructokinase activity.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une bactérie de type corynebacterium ayant une activité 6-phosphofructokinase améliorée dans la cellule et capable de produire de la L-lysine. L'invention concerne en outre un procédé relatif à l'élaboration de L-lysine, qui consiste à mettre en culture la bactérie considérée dans un milieu afin de constituer et d'accumuler la L-lysine à l'intérieur de ce milieu, et qui consiste enfin à recueillir la L-lysine dans le même milieu. L'invention concerne également de l'ADN qui peut être utilisé pour améliorer l'activité 6-phosphofructokinase.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>